<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Life of Saint Severinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">511</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Vita Sancti Severini, Commemoratorium vitae Sancti Severini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Life of Saint Severinus is a biography of the monk Severinus of Noricum written by his disciple <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugippius">Eugippius</a> in 511. It describes life in the Roman towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> province of Noricum in the late 5th century, under the pressure of the Rugians and other barbarian peoples, and the evacuation of the Roman population to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 488. It is the main source for the end of Roman rule in the region.</p></div>
